---
title: Sitemap
layout: home
description: Every page on the site as one tree, generated from the same array the navigation is built from — so it cannot drift out of date.
eyebrow: Pages
source: src/components/sitemap.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap im-pt-sm im-section-sm">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Pages · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<section class="im-section im-wrap-wide">
	<div class="im-collbar">
		<p class="im-caption im-m0" data-index="tree">Everything</p>
		<p class="im-snipcard-meta"><span>{{sitemap.length}} sections</span><a class="im-card-cta" href="/sitemap.xml">sitemap.xml {{icon "external-link"}}</a></p>
	</div>

	<nav class="im-sitetree" aria-label="Sitemap">
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a class="im-sitetree-node im-sitetree-root" href="/">{{icon "globe"}}{{name}}</a>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<span class="im-sitetree-node im-sitetree-branch">{{icon "file-text"}}Pages <small>9</small></span>
						<ul>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/home/">{{icon "house"}}Home</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/about/">{{icon "user"}}About</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/resume/">{{icon "briefcase"}}Résumé</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/guestbook/">{{icon "pencil"}}Guestbook</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/now/">{{icon "clock"}}Now</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/contact/">{{icon "mail"}}Contact</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/membership/" data-locked>{{icon "credit-card"}}Membership</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/auth/">{{icon "log-in"}}Sign in / Sign up</a></li>
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="/pages/sitemap/">{{icon "list"}}Sitemap</a></li>
						</ul>
					</li>
					{{#each sitemap}}
					{{#unless title}}{{#each items}}<li><a class="im-sitetree-node im-sitetree-branch" href="{{url}}">{{icon icon}}{{label}}</a></li>{{/each}}{{else}}
					<li>
						<span class="im-sitetree-node im-sitetree-branch">{{icon icon}}{{title}} <small>{{count}}</small></span>
						<ul>
							{{#each items}}
							{{#if children}}
							<li>
								<a class="im-sitetree-node im-sitetree-branch" href="{{children.[0].url}}">{{icon icon}}{{label}} <small>{{children.length}}</small></a>
								<ul>{{#each children}}<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a></li>{{/each}}</ul>
							</li>
							{{else}}
							<li><a class="im-sitetree-node" href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a></li>
							{{/if}}
							{{/each}}
						</ul>
					</li>
					{{/unless}}
					{{/each}}
				</ul>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</nav>
</section>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>Generated, not written</h2>
		<p>The tree above iterates the <em>same array</em> the side navigation is built from. Adding a page adds a row here and there is nothing to remember — which is the only kind of sitemap that stays true, because a hand-written one is wrong within a month and then actively misleads.</p>

		<h2>A tree that branches</h2>
		<p>Every parent sits level with the middle of its children, and each child hangs off one spine by a short arm. The spine is two half-lines per child — above and below its own middle — so it starts at the first child and stops at the last without anything being measured. Nothing folds: the whole site is on the page at once. Under 48rem the same list grows downward instead of sideways.</p>
		<h2>Two sitemaps, two readers</h2>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th></th><th>This page</th><th><code>sitemap.xml</code></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><th>For</th><td>A person who is lost</td><td>A crawler</td></tr>
				<tr><th>Shows</th><td>Structure, grouped, with counts</td><td>Every URL, flat, with dates</td></tr>
				<tr><th>In Ghost</th><td>A page on the theme</td><td>Generated by Ghost, no theme involved</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
		<p>Both should exist and neither replaces the other. Link the XML one from here, as above — it is the only place on a site where that link is useful to anybody.</p>

		<h2>Marking what is behind the wall</h2>
		<p><code>data-locked</code> on a node draws a small lock after the label. A sitemap that silently lists members-only pages sends people to a gate without warning them; one that hides them is lying about what the site contains.</p>
		<p>Classes: <code>im-sitetree</code> (a plain nested list), <code>im-sitetree-node</code>, <code>im-sitetree-branch</code> (a folder), <code>im-sitetree-root</code>. Knobs: <code>--im-tree-arm</code>, <code>--im-tree-gap</code>, <code>--im-tree-line</code>.</p>
	</div>
</section>
